  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes:\u00a0*Via per Alpes Numidicas</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Fowler discusses a fragmentary Roman milestone found along the road from Hippo to Calama that mentions a \"Via per Alpes Numidicas\". The Clauss / Slaby epigraphic database (EDCS-04001742) lists the findspot as Ain Berda in the province of Africa proconsularis and dates the inscription to ca. 150 CE.",
